---
{
  title: "manhattan_distance"
}
---
### NAME

    manhattan_distance() - Calculates the Manhattan distance between two
    points: the number of steps between them when movement runs along the
    axes only, with no diagonals. Points may have any number of axes, so 2D
    and 3D coordinates both work.

### SYNOPSIS

    int manhattan_distance( int *a, int *b );

### DESCRIPTION

    Calculates the Manhattan distance between two points: the number of
    steps between them when movement runs along the axes only, with no
    diagonals. Points may have any number of axes, so 2D and 3D coordinates
    both work.

### PARAMETERS

    a  (int*)
       The first point's coordinates.

    b  (int*)
       The second point's coordinates, in the same axis order as `a`.

### RETURN VALUES

    (int) The sum of the absolute differences along each axis.

### ERRORS

    If either point is not a non-empty array of integers. If the points have
    different numbers of axes.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}manhattan_distance(({ 0, 2, 3 }), ({ 0, 5, 1 })) // 5{{di0}}
